   "source": [
    "# Sentiment Analysis of Amazon Product Reviews\n",
    "\n",
    "In this project I analyse Amazon product reviews to understand customer sentiment.\n",
    "I use Python for cleaning and analysis, export the data to Excel where I apply text functions and create a pivot table, and then train a Naive Bayes model to predict whether a review is positive or negative.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** Amazon India product reviews (downloaded from course materials)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6e2f7a04",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 – Import libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "76394481",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3c1f5f7c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 – Load the data\n",
    "\n",
    "The CSV has one row per product with multiple reviews packed into a single cell separated by commas.\n",
    "I need to split them out so each row is one review.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dce9880a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv('amazon.csv')\n",
    "print('Shape:', df_raw.shape)\n",
    "df_raw.head(3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1492b67a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for _, row in df_raw.iterrows():\n",
    "    titles   = [t.strip() for t in str(row['review_title']).split(',')]\n",
    "    contents = [c.strip() for c in str(row['review_content']).split(',')]\n",
    "    n = max(len(titles), len(contents))\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in range(n):\n",
    "        rows.append({\n",
    "            'product' : str(row['product_name'])[:60],\n",
    "            'category': str(row['category']).split('|')[0],\n",
    "            'rating'  : str(row['rating']),\n",
    "            'title'   : titles[i]   if i < len(titles)   else '',\n",
    "            'review'  : contents[i] if i < len(contents) else '',\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "print('Total reviews:', len(df))\n",
    "df.head(5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f5643d8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 – Clean the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6d88dd05",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Missing values:')\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4d9ab82b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert rating from string to float\n",
    "def parse_rating(r):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        val = float(str(r).strip())\n",
    "        if 1 <= val <= 5:\n",
    "            return val\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "df['rating'] = df['rating'].apply(parse_rating)\n",
    "df = df.dropna(subset=['rating'])\n",
    "print('Rows after cleaning:', len(df))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "559fd9aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Combine title and review text\n",
    "df['review_text'] = (df['title'] + ' ' + df['review']).str.strip()\n",
    "df = df[df['review_text'].str.len() > 5].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add sentiment label\n",
    "def get_sentiment(r):\n",
    "    if r >= 4:\n",
    "        return 'Positive'\n",
    "    elif r <= 2:\n",
    "        return 'Negative'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Neutral'\n",
    "\n",
    "df['sentiment']      = df['rating'].apply(get_sentiment)\n",
    "df['review_length']  = df['review_text'].apply(len)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df['sentiment'].value_counts())\n",
    "df.head(5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5b353689",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 – Export to Excel\n",
    "\n",
    "I export the cleaned data to Excel. The file will have two sheets:\n",
    "- **Reviews** – the cleaned dataset (I will add formulas to this manually in Excel)\n",
    "- **Word Frequency** – frequency count of positive vs negative words\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "182f1f8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "positive_words = [\n",
    "    'good', 'great', 'excellent', 'amazing', 'perfect', 'love', 'best',\n",
    "    'fantastic', 'awesome', 'quality', 'happy', 'recommend', 'satisfied',\n",
    "    'wonderful', 'nice', 'easy', 'fast', 'reliable', 'value', 'superb'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "negative_words = [\n",
    "    'bad', 'terrible', 'awful', 'worst', 'horrible', 'broke', 'broken',\n",
    "    'waste', 'poor', 'disappointed', 'slow', 'cheap', 'fake', 'useless',\n",
    "    'damaged', 'defective', 'problem', 'issue', 'failed', 'return'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count how many reviews contain each word\n",
    "pos_freq = {w: int(df['review_text'].str.lower().str.contains(w).sum()) for w in positive_words}\n",
    "neg_freq = {w: int(df['review_text'].str.lower().str.contains(w).sum()) for w in negative_words}\n",
    "\n",
    "pos_df = pd.DataFrame(list(pos_freq.items()), columns=['word', 'count']).sort_values('count', ascending=False)\n",
    "neg_df = pd.DataFrame(list(neg_freq.items()), columns=['word', 'count']).sort_values('count', ascending=False)\n",
    "pos_df['type'] = 'Positive'\n",
    "neg_df['type'] = 'Negative'\n",
    "\n",
    "word_freq_df = pd.concat([pos_df, neg_df], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Word frequency table:')\n",
    "print(word_freq_df.head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4f50f8bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Export to Excel\n",
    "excel_path = 'amazon_reviews.xlsx'\n",
    "\n",
    "with pd.ExcelWriter(excel_path, engine='openpyxl') as writer:\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Sheet 1: Reviews (first 1000 rows so the file stays manageable)\n",
    "    df[['product', 'category', 'rating', 'sentiment', 'review_text', 'review_length']].head(1000).to_excel(\n",
    "        writer, sheet_name='Reviews', index=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Sheet 2: Word frequency count\n",
    "    word_freq_df.to_excel(writer, sheet_name='Word Frequency', index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Saved: {excel_path}')"
   ]
  },
